From: Halcyon Browser Project <halcyon@local>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] webui: Register Halcyon NTP (the Plume) at chrome://newtab

This patch replaces the upstream chrome://newtab WebUI registration with
the Halcyon Plume. The Plume lives in chrome/browser/resources/halcyon_ntp/
and is served by the HalcyonNtpUI controller in chrome/browser/ui/webui/

When `enable_halcyon` is true (the default in the Halcyon build), the
Plume is registered. When false, the upstream NTP is left untouched.

The patch is intentionally minimal — the only thing it changes is the
WebUI controller class that gets registered for the `chrome::kChromeUINewTabHost`
URL. The Plume's HTML/CSS/JS and the HalcyonNtpMessageHandler are entirely
new files (no upstream modification).

Applies cleanly against Chromium at the time of writing (November 2026).
If the surrounding code has shifted, the manual change is:
  in chrome/browser/ui/webui/webui_configurations.cc,
  find the block:
    WebUIConfigurations::RegisterURLLoader(...)
  and within it, change the NewTab registration to create
  `new halcyon::HalcyonNtpUI()` instead of the upstream NewTabUI.

---
 chrome/browser/ui/webui/webui_configurations.cc | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/webui/webui_configurations.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/webui/webui_configurations.cc
index 0000000..1111111 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/webui/webui_configurations.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/webui/webui_configurations.cc
@@ -100,6 +100,7 @@
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/webui/bookmarks/bookmarks_ui.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/webui/new_tab/new_tab_ui.h"
+#include "chrome/browser/ui/webui/halcyon_ntp_ui.h"

 namespace chrome {

@@ -233,7 +234,12 @@ void WebUIConfigurations::RegisterURLLoader(
   // chrome://newtab
-  RegisterWebUIConfig<NewTabUI>(chrome::kChromeUINewTabHost);
+  if (base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(features::kHalcyonUI)) {
+    RegisterWebUIConfig<halcyon::HalcyonNtpUI>(chrome::kChromeUINewTabHost);
+  } else {
+    RegisterWebUIConfig<NewTabUI>(chrome::kChromeUINewTabHost);
+  }
+
   // chrome://settings
   RegisterWebUIConfig<SettingsUI>(chrome::kChromeUISettingsHost);
   // chrome://history
